      "writtenOn": "2021-07-22T18:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a small list of these associated with each release. Long term the subsys would:\n1. Have a Kconfig that gives us the path to the CHRE project (in our case it would be src/third_party/chre)\n2. Check the version of the CHRE we\u0027re building (this would be upstream to allow people to build against different versions). Then load CMake rules specific to that version.\n\nCurrently I believe that there are only a handfull of these that need to be done (roughly in the order of 5-7 from scanning over code-search).\n\nIdeally, long term, CHRE would support the builds internally and we wouldn\u0027t need to have these wrappers. Though even with their current release cadence, these wrappers should be fairly minimal.",
      "parentUuid": "4debbc22_bc026fce",
      "revId": "0bc3ecc885ebf3f27e35dfe6487af70950fda5f8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
